 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.987,
   "text": "Today: What Is a Fraction?"
  },
  {
   "start": 2.287,
   "end": 5.46,
   "text": "Here's what we'll cover. First: Parts of a Whole."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.61,
   "end": 7.835,
   "text": "Second: The Top and the Bottom."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.985,
   "end": 10.196,
   "text": "Third: Comparing Fractions."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.346,
   "end": 12.921,
   "text": "And finally: Equal Fractions."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.221,
   "end": 15.275,
   "text": "Part 1: Parts of a Whole."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.425,
   "end": 20.02,
   "text": "Imagine you have a pizza, and you cut it into four equal slices."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.02,
   "end": 24.095,
   "text": "Each slice is one part of the whole pizza. We call that one fourth,"
  },
  {
   "start": 24.095,
   "end": 26.198,
   "text": "and we write it as one over four."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.348,
   "end": 31.665,
   "text": "A fraction is a way of showing a part of something that has been split into equal pieces."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.965,
   "end": 35.896,
   "text": "Key takeaway: Each slice is one part of the whole pizza."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.446,
   "end": 38.831,
   "text": "Part 2: The Top and the Bottom."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.981,
   "end": 43.829,
   "text": "Every fraction has two numbers. The bottom number is called the denominator."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.829,
   "end": 47.379,
   "text": "It tells you how many equal pieces the whole is cut into."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.379,
   "end": 49.754,
   "text": "The top number is called the numerator."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.754,
   "end": 53.004,
   "text": "It tells you how many of those pieces you are talking about."
  },
  {
   "start": 53.004,
   "end": 56.243,
   "text": "So three over four means three slices out of four."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.643,
   "end": 59.858,
   "text": "Key takeaway: Every fraction has two numbers."
  },
  {
   "start": 60.408,
   "end": 62.823,
   "text": "Part 3: Comparing Fractions."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.973,
   "end": 66.842,
   "text": "Which is bigger, one half or one fourth? Think about the pizza."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.842,
   "end": 70.042,
   "text": "If you cut it into two slices, each slice is big."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.042,
   "end": 73.367,
   "text": "If you cut it into four slices, each slice is smaller."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.367,
   "end": 79.296,
   "text": "So one half is bigger than one fourth. When the denominator gets bigger, each piece gets smaller."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.596,
   "end": 84.199,
   "text": "Key takeaway: If you cut it into four slices, each slice is smaller."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.749,
   "end": 87.048,
   "text": "Part 4: Equal Fractions."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.198,
   "end": 90.997,
   "text": "Two halves make a whole, and so do four fourths. Also,"
  },
  {
   "start": 90.997,
   "end": 94.872,
   "text": "one half is the same amount as two fourths. They look different,"
  },
  {
   "start": 94.872,
   "end": 99.158,
   "text": "but they cover the same space. We call these equivalent fractions."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.458,
   "end": 104.169,
   "text": "Key takeaway: Also, one half is the same amount as two fourths."
  },
  {
   "start": 104.719,
   "end": 108.606,
   "text": "A fraction tells us how many equal parts we have out of the whole."
  },
  {
   "start": 108.606,
   "end": 111.361,
   "text": "The bottom number counts the pieces in the whole,"
  },
  {
   "start": 111.361,
   "end": 114.136,
   "text": "and the top number counts the pieces we have."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.136,
   "end": 117.166,
   "text": "Now you can share a pizza fairly with your friends."
  },
  {
   "start": 117.416,
   "end": 119.056,
   "text": "Thanks for watching!"
  }
 ],
